\title{textscale: Measure Latent Quantities from Text Using Pairwise Comparisons}
\description{
Implements a method for measuring latent quantities (e.g., ideology, ad tone, argument persuasiveness) from text by combining text embeddings with pairwise comparisons. Pairwise annotations — generated by human annotators or a large language model — identify a latent dimension in embedding space. An L2-regularized logistic regression model is then fit on embedding differences, enabling efficient scoring of new documents without additional pairwise annotations.
